  "content": "## Giving data is pastoral\n\nDonor names, emails, addresses, and gift amounts are pastoral data. Reduce\ninside `execute_code`: page, filter, and total there, and return the\naggregate (sums by fund, month, or donor count), not donor rows, unless the\ntask needs named people.\n\n## Ids and joins\n\n- Ids carry their kind: `org_` organization, `user_` donor account, `ch_`\n  charge, `rc_` recurring gift, `pm_` payment method. Read them from the list\n  tools; never guess one.\n- Tithe.ly lists charges and recurring gifts only for one organization or one\n  donor, so pass `organizationId` or `accountId`.\n- A charge carries its donor's name and email, its organization's name, and\n  its payment method, so most joins need no second read.\n- `list_accounts` covers every account these keys can see; `scope: \"api\"`\n  narrows it to accounts created through this API.\n- The named reads project Tithe.ly's records. A field a projection omits, such\n  as an account's phone and postal address, comes back from `tithely_api_read`\n  on that record's path.\n\n## Money, dates and funds\n\n- A fund is a Tithe.ly giving type: `giving_type` in Tithe.ly's records,\n  `fund` in projections.\n- Projections give amounts as integer `…Cents` and dates as ISO 8601 UTC\n  `…At`. Tithe.ly's own records, from `tithely_api_read`, keep string cents\n  and Unix seconds.\n- `depositedAt` may be `\"pending\"`. There is no deposits resource: net amount\n  and fees live on each charge.\n- A charge a recurring gift produced has `recurring: true`; a one-time gift\n  has `recurring: false`.\n\n## Writes\n\n- Every write moves money or changes a donor's records. Bodies are form\n  fields in integer cents and Unix seconds.\n- `POST /refunds/{charge_id}` refunds a whole charge.\n  `DELETE /recurring/{recurring_id}` stops future charges and refunds nothing.\n- Card and bank tokens, which `POST /charge-once` and `POST /payment-methods`\n  need, come only from Tithely.js in a donor's browser. An agent cannot\n  create one.\n- Tithe.ly reports most refusals as HTTP 200 with `status: \"fail\"` and a\n  reason but no code. They arrive as `connector_call_failed`; read the reason\n  before deciding what to do next.\n\n## Not available\n\nOnly Tithe.ly's API v1 is reachable; its undocumented v2 is not.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** while `page.hasMore` is true, continue with `page.nextCursor` unchanged. For `list_accounts`, `list_charges`, `list_organizations`, `list_payment_methods`, `list_recurring_charges`, `tithely_api_details`, `tithely_api_search`, pass it as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw paging anchors on continuations. Keep the original method, path, filters, page size, fields and headers. Paged `list_*` and `search_*` reads take `limit` (default 25, at most 99). The last page has no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation was withheld. When approaching execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor before the call that would exceed it and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `tithely_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `tithely_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `tithely_api_read` calls a reviewed read. Details' `response.fields` promises selection only; `withheld` hints are incomplete, and absence never means safe or readable. `tithely_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. An unknown id, or one these credentials cannot reach, fails as `connector_call_failed`; this API does not tell the two apart. It documents no conflict.\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
